  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Deathly power fills a 60-foot Emanation originating from you for the duration.</p><p>When you cast this spell, you can choose creatures it doesn’t affect. Any other creature can’t regain Hit Points while in the Emanation. Whenever the Emanation enters a creature’s space, and whenever a creature enters it or ends its turn there, the creature makes a Constitution saving throw, no more than once per turn. On a failure, it takes 3d10 Necrotic damage and has the &amp;Reference[prone apply=false]{Prone} condition; on a success, it takes half as much damage and its Speed is halved.</p><p><strong>Casting as a Circle Spell.</strong> Casting this as a Circle spell requires at least two secondary casters, and its duration becomes Concentration, up to 10 minutes. A creature that fails its save against the spell also gains 1 &amp;Reference[exhaustion apply=false]{Exhaustion} level, and while it has Exhaustion levels, finishing a Long Rest neither restores its lost Hit Points nor reduces its Exhaustion level. When the spell is cast, each secondary caster must expend a level 4+ spell slot; otherwise, the spell fails.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-LBz1hE0yvqIA1IL0\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>The halved Speed of a success lasts until the end of the turn.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
